# AGENTS.md

Guidance for AI coding agents working in this repository — a **<%= @title %>**
app built on [Izen](https://github.com/adiprnm/izen), a lightweight,
module-first core for Roda + SQLite.

## What this is

Izen is plain Ruby: **no ORM**, **no autoloader**, **no framework magic**.
Persistence is raw SQL over SQLite, and every file is required explicitly.

## Commands

```sh
bundle install
bundle exec izen dev [--port PORT] [--host HOST]  # boot the dev server (rackup/Puma)
bundle exec izen migration migrate                # apply all pending migrations
bundle exec izen migration rollback [STEP]        # roll back the last STEP (default 1)
bundle exec izen migration status                 # show applied / pending
bundle exec izen migration generate NAME          # write an empty up/down pair
bundle exec izen module new NAME field:type ...   # scaffold a domain module
bundle exec rake test                             # run the test suite
bundle exec izen native build                     # compile one native binary (Spinel)
```

`APP_ENV` selects the environment (defaults to `development`; tests use `test`).

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app.rb` | Roda application, requires `app/*/*.rb` and declares routes |
| `app/<module>/` | A domain module: model, contract, repository, controller, views, colocated tests |
| `app/layout.erb` | Shared ERB layout |
| `migrations/` | Versioned `NNNNNN_name.up.sql` / `.down.sql` migrations |
| `config/database.yaml` | SQLite path per `APP_ENV` |
| `config/storage.yml` | Upload storage service per `APP_ENV` (default: `local`) |
| `storage/` | SQLite databases, the session secret and uploaded files |
| `test/` | App-level tests and the native conformance scenarios |

## Conventions

### Modules

`izen module new post title:string body:text` creates a module with four
layers. The **module name is singular**; the SQL table and routes are plural.

- **Model** (`Base::Model`) — a typed value object, no persistence:
  `attribute :title, String`, `attribute :body, String`.
- **Contract** (`Base::Contract`) — params validation:
  `params { required :title, String; optional :body, String }`. `#call` returns
  a result with `success?`, `to_h` and `errors`.
- **Repository** (`Base::Repository`) — *all* database access, raw SQL:
  `query`, `find_one`, `to_model`, `to_models`, `transaction`.
- **Controller** (`Base::Controller`) — orchestrates the request, renders views
  and sets flash messages.

Data flow:

- read: `controller -> repository -> view`
- write: `controller -> contract -> model -> repository -> view`

### Views

ERB files live next to the module (`app/<module>/index.erb`, `show.erb`,
`new.erb`, `edit.erb`) and render inside `app/layout.erb`.

### Uploads

Store uploaded files with `Izen::Storage`, which writes through the service
named in `config/storage.yml` (default: `local`, under `storage/uploads`,
served at `/uploads`):

```ruby
key = Izen::Storage.store(params["avatar"]) # => "2026/10/ab12….png"
Izen::Storage.url(key)                      # => "/uploads/2026/10/ab12….png"
```

Persist the returned key in the database and derive the URL from it. `store`
accepts a Rack multipart hash, an uploaded-file object, a File/IO or a path.
Swap the service (e.g. for an S3-compatible bucket) in `config/storage.yml`
without changing callers; S3 credentials belong in the `S3_*` env vars.

### Routes

Routes are declared in `app.rb` inside the `route` block. `izen module new`
inserts the module's routes just above the `# cli:module-routes` marker, so
leave that marker in place.

### Migrations

Add schema changes as a versioned `up`/`down` pair under `migrations/`. Use
`izen migration generate NAME` (or `izen module new`, which writes the create
migration) and run `izen migration migrate`.

### Tests

Minitest. Colocate `*_test.rb` with the module under `app/<module>/`.

- `TestSupport::DatabaseTest` runs each test in a transaction that is rolled
  back afterwards.
- `TestSupport::ControllerTest` adds `Rack::Test` against `App`.

## Rules

- **No autoloader.** `app.rb` requires every `app/*/*.rb` file (skipping
  `*_test.rb`). New modules under `app/` are picked up automatically; code in a
  new top-level directory is not.
- Keep SQL inside repositories and validation inside contracts.
- Never commit `.env`, SQLite databases, `/storage/session_secret`, uploaded
  files under `/storage/uploads`, or `/config/deploy*.yml` (all git-ignored).
- Configuration lives in `config/database.yaml`, `config/storage.yml`, and
  `.env` (loaded by `Izen::Dotenv`). Both YAML files are ERB-rendered, so
  values can come from the environment (`<%%= ENV["S3_BUCKET"] %>`).
